**Current state:** Only one experiment exists — high polymer (17 wt%), cold bath (5°C), mid pullcast speed (10 mm/s), N₂ blow, short wait (30s), minimum bath time (1200s), mixing at 25°C (required at max polymer). The fit quality was poor (43/100), suggesting the mechanical response was not well-captured, but the membrane itself was physically intact.

**Explore strategy — move far from the existing point across multiple dimensions:**

1. **polymer_wt:** Drop significantly from 17.0 → try **13.0 wt%**. Lower polymer concentration will produce a more open, less dense structure — very different morphology. This also frees up `mixing_temp` to be varied.
